  "limitations": [
    "SCHED-05 starts with one exact separately committed active and unexpired SCHED-02 claim; it does not move claim acquisition into the processing transaction.",
    "SCHED-04 remains authoritative for deterministic claim-time misfire classification and bounded next-occurrence planning; SCHED-05 persists that immutable plan rather than recalculating from later processing time.",
    "A rolled-back processing attempt intentionally leaves the original due time, version, and active lease unchanged. SCHED-06 owns strict-expiry discovery, reclaim, restart races, and duplicate suppression after recovery or response loss.",
    "Stable uniqueness and atomic receipt prove one committed occurrence and receipt for this exact live claim, not exactly-once Run execution.",
    "Runtime evidence uses file-backed SQLite and injected time without sleeps. PostgreSQL DDL and constraints compile, but PostgreSQL runtime locking and contention are not exercised.",
